1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,666
WITNESS — post-code automation. One rule: an empty result
and a failed request are not the same thing.

2
00:00:09,816 --> 00:00:24,278
An agent that writes code can also misreport what
happened. The dangerous failure is a confident, wrong
success message.

3
00:00:24,428 --> 00:00:53,913
Four frames. One absence is not a withdrawal. A failed
request is not an offline device. Only the fourth frame
asserts a withdrawal.

4
00:00:54,063 --> 00:01:08,779
A green tick says the jobs exited zero. It does not say
the claim was exercised. The submission is the automation.

5
00:01:08,929 --> 00:01:36,394
Three Duo Agent Platform flows, three levels of autonomy:
assisted, supervised, hands-off.

6
00:01:36,544 --> 00:02:00,990
Nine stages. The last stage classifies every claim:
VERIFIED / DOCUMENTED / UNVERIFIED / UNAVAILABLE. It does
not print a green tick.

7
00:02:01,140 --> 00:02:17,076
396 tests pass with no credential. The ledger verifier
rejects five tamper classes. All of it is in the public
project.

8
00:02:17,226 --> 00:02:41,532
The honest limit: the hands-off merge is refused by the
flow's own credential, and the flow reports that rather
than routing around it.

9
00:02:41,682 --> 00:02:56,829
Path B. The product is pre-existing and MIT licensed. The
automation is new work. Every claim is checkable in the
public repo.
